# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `make SANITIZE=thread tsan-test`
# (.github/workflows/tsan.yml). Every entry says why it is not a CWIST bug.
#
# sqlite3_backup_init() locks the source and then the destination database.
# NukeDB backs up disk -> memory when it loads and memory -> disk when it
# syncs, so TSan sees both lock orders. The two never overlap: the load runs
# in cwist_nuke_init() before the sync thread starts, and the final sync in
# cwist_nuke_close() runs after that thread is joined.
deadlock:sqlite3_backup_init

# libttak's retired-node pool (lib/libttak/src/mem/epoch.c) pops a lock-free
# Treiber stack: a popper reads head->next while another popper that won the
# same head clears it. Nodes are never freed, so this does not crash, but it
# is an ABA hazard in the vendored library, not in CWIST code. It needs a fix
# in libttak and a submodule bump; tracked in issue #351. Intermittent, so
# without this entry the TSan job would fail at random.
race:epoch_node_pool_acquire
